      mLameKO: 'Could not load the MP3 encoder (connection?): pick WAV or try again.', mNote: 'Tracks are read from your own disc and converted in your browser. The MP3 encoder (lamejs, LGPL) is loaded from jsDelivr the first time. The BGM… names are the disc’s own file names.',
      tabProg: 'Progress', tabProgSub: 'Your 100% checklist, read from your memory card',
      tabPatch: 'Patches', tabPatchSub: 'The Remix hack: hidden riders, tricks, MAX…',
      heroLead: 'The Remix hack, repainted outfits and your own board for Cool Boarders 2. Everything runs in your browser from your own game: no game files are hosted here.',
      chip1: '❄ Remix patch v{v}', chip2: '3D skins', chip3: 'Custom boards', dropSmall: '.chd, .bin or .img — the file stays on your computer', heroCap: 'Remix v{v}: SSX Style Boost, Jicchi, Nick, Kelly, Snowman…',
      badgeNew: 'New', showCta: 'Patch my game', ctaPatch: 'Patch my game', ctaNews: 'See what’s new',
      showTitle: 'What the <span>Remix</span> changes',
      showLead: 'The Cool Boarders 2 you know, with everything it was missing: hidden riders finally playable, a real boost, a ranking you can read mid-race… and it is all set in the game.',
      fk_boost: "Race",
      ft_boost: "SSX Style Boost",
      fp_boost: "Your tricks turn into speed.",
      fd_boost: "In the original Cool Boarders 2, a trick in the Boarder Cross earned you nothing. Now every air, every grab, every spin fills your meter, in the colour of your rider’s jacket. Land clean to bank it, botch the landing and it is gone. Then hit R2: you smoothly speed up to 40 % faster, a light trail behind your board and speed lines all around. Take risks, overtake everyone.",
      fk_crew: "Riders",
      ft_crew: "Jicchi, Nick and Kelly, finally playable",
      fp_crew: "The riders who beat you now race for you.",
      fd_crew: "Since 1998 they were only computer opponents. The Remix gives them a spot on the select screen, with their head, their real stats, their voice (deeper or higher) and their icons in the results. The perfect reward once you have finished everything at 100 %.",
      fk_riders: "Riders",
      ft_riders: "Boss, Gray and Snowman in the championship",
      fp_riders: "The bonus riders leave the locker room.",
      fd_riders: "You unlocked them for… Free Style. Here they race the whole Competition, Big Air and Boarder Cross included. Snowman has his real animations, his skeleton put back together and his own voice; Gray has his too. A podium with a snowman is priceless.",
      fk_radar: "Race",
      ft_radar: "A Mario Kart style ranking",
      fp_radar: "Always know who is ahead, and by how much.",
      fd_radar: "On the right: your place, the rider ahead and the one behind, with their head and the gap in seconds (shimmering gold, silver and bronze for the podium). At the bottom: a long line with every rider’s head moving along. No more guessing: you see the race.",
      fk_falls: "Race",
      ft_falls: "Your falls at a glance",
      fp_falls: "One ball, one number: x13.",
      fd_falls: "The original falls counter lined up big and small balls at the bottom of the screen. The Remix moves it to the top left, as a single number if you like. Easier to read, and it makes room for the radar.",
      fk_ramming: "Race",
      ft_ramming: "Boarder Cross ramming",
      fp_ramming: "Slam into them: the faster one stays up.",
      fd_ramming: "In the original game, touching an opponent did nothing. With the Remix, if you hit him faster than he goes, he is the one sent into the powder. Overtaking gets physical, and you have to watch the riders coming from behind too.",
      fk_remix: "Game",
      ft_remix: "Your Remix, set in the game",
      fp_remix: "A real options screen, in the game’s style.",
      fd_remix: "Under the OPTIONS sign, the REMIX logo opens a screen in three tabs (Race, Riders, Game). Switch each mod on or off from the pad, without patching your game again, and your choice stays in your save.",
      fk_ws: "Game",
      ft_ws: "16:9 widescreen",
      fp_ws: "The whole width of your TV.",
      fd_ws: "A REMIX screen option widens the view for a 16:9 screen: more course on the left and right, without white edges or missing scenery. Use it with the picture stretched to 16:9 in the emulator or on the TV.",
      fk_rear: "Race",
      ft_rear: "Rear view",
      fp_rear: "See who is right on your tail.",
      fd_rear: "Hold Circle in a race and the camera turns around: you see the riders coming up behind you, even in the big descents. Let go and you are back on your line.",
      fk_air: "Race",
      ft_air: "Air control",
      fp_air: "Save your spins before you touch the snow.",
      fd_air: "In the air, the d-pad in the direction of your spin speeds it up, the other way slows it down to land straight. Tricks work as usual, but you land far more often, so you go bigger.",
      fk_hplive: "Half-pipe",
      ft_hplive: "Live half-pipe marks",
      fp_hplive: "The judges score you while you ride.",
      fd_hplive: "No need to wait for the end of the run: the marks (manoeuvres, amplitude, landing, rotation, technical merit) show and climb trick after trick. You know at once what pays off.",
      fk_bam: "Big Air",
      ft_bam: "Big Air Master, finally readable",
      fp_bam: "You always know what comes next.",
      fd_bam: "The keys of the requested trick stay on screen, the next tricks (NEXT) are listed on the right, and Exit in the pause ends the session with your score and ranking.",
      fk_outfits: "Riders",
      ft_outfits: "The girls’ hidden outfits",
      fp_outfits: "Outfits that were asleep on the disc.",
      fd_outfits: "Cindy and Irin have outfits the game never showed. The Remix makes them available on the select screen.",
      fk_max: "Riders",
      ft_max: "Riders and board at MAX",
      fp_max: "Every bar maxed out.",
      fd_max: "A MAX rider and board: jump, balance, technique, speed, all maxed. And the SPECIAL boards everywhere. For the runs where you just want to go fast.",
      fk_hardmirror: "Game",
      ft_hardmirror: "The Hard + Mirror championship",
      fp_hardmirror: "The ultimate challenge: hard, and mirrored.",
      fd_hardmirror: "A new Competition mixing Hard difficulty and mirrored courses. Start it with L1 + R1 + X on Competition, as soon as Hard is unlocked.",
      fk_news: "Game",
      ft_news: "Unlock announcements",
      fp_news: "You finally know what you just won.",
      fd_news: "Back from a race, a shining message tells you what you just unlocked: a rider, a trophy, a course… Nothing goes unnoticed anymore.",
      fk_progress: "Game",
      ft_progress: "The progress page",
      fp_progress: "Your road to 100 %.",
      fd_progress: "SELECT on the mode select screen: your percentage, what is done, what is left and how to get it (riders, Mirror, Hard, boards, the 30 Free Style trophies).",
      fk_skipq: "Race",
      ft_skipq: "Skip qualifying",
      fp_skipq: "Straight to the Boarder Cross.",
      fd_skipq: "With SELECT you skip the 1st stage trick event and start the Boarder Cross from a place mid-pack. Perfect to chain races.",
      fk_unlock: "Game",
      ft_unlock: "Unlock everything at once",
      fp_unlock: "To play everything right away.",
      fd_unlock: "In the REMIX screen, UNLOCK EVERYTHING unlocks riders, courses, boards, Mirror, Hard and trophies, and writes it to your save. Or keep the fun of earning it all yourself: your call.",
      chooseTitle: 'Pick your workshop', needDisc: 'Open your game in step 1 first.', otherDisc: 'Change game',
